Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:53:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] WLANRTSYS-102892 : ACS add acs_bootup_non_dfs and
 acs_bootup_non_dfs_allow_exclusion for 5G non-DFS bootup channel selection

During initial 5G bootup, ACS may select a DFS channel which requires CAC
before traffic can flow, causing delays for the user. Two new mutually
exclusive config options address this:

- acs_bootup_non_dfs=1: initial ACS picks a non-DFS channel; a one-shot
  15-min timer (ACS_BOOTUP_NON_DFS_TIMER_SECS=900s) then re-evaluates
  with DFS channels included and switches if a better channel is found.
  bgACS is deferred until the timer fires.

- acs_bootup_non_dfs_allow_exclusion=1: same non-DFS bootup behaviour AND
  the opclass exclusion list is hard-applied during that phase. bgACS
  starts immediately; exclusion-list switches are allowed but DFS channels
  remain excluded until the timer fires.

Fixup :  WLANRTSYS-50170 [MXL] Smart ACS implementation
